    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "rural_communities_description",
      "value": "Rural communities are found in villages and small towns, where life tends to be slower, and people have close-knit relationships. In these areas, families often know each other for generations, and social life revolves around traditions, festivals and local gatherings. Agriculture, fishing, and small-scale industries are usually the backbone of the local economy. While rural communities have a strong sense of togetherness, they can also struggle with limited access to healthcare, education and job opportunities. A good example would be a farming village in India, where people help each other during harvest season and celebrate cultural festivals together.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": {
        "source_type": "page",
        "source_id": null,
        "title": "Types of Communities",
        "url": null
      },
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0005",
        "chunk_title": "Types of Communities",
        "chunk_order": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "urban_communities_description",
      "value": "Urban communities exist in cities, where life moves at a much faster pace. People in urban areas come from diverse backgrounds and work in a variety of professions. While cities offer more opportunities in terms of jobs, education and entertainment, they can also be overwhelming, with problems like overcrowding, pollution, and expensive living costs. Unlike rural areas, relationships in urban communities are often more formal and less personal. However, cities also have strong neighbourhood cultures, where people form smaller, local communities within the larger urban environment. Think of a bustling Mumbai neighbourhood where people from different cultural backgrounds live side by side, interacting through work, school, and social events.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": {
        "source_type": "page",
        "source_id": null,
        "title": "Types of Communities",
        "url": null
      },
